# name: test_build_started_dispatches_when_no_builder_exists
  '''
  IMPORTANT: This output is an execution script. Follow it verbatim.
  
  INVARIANT: Never invoke the next state-machine call (telec todo prepare/work/integrate) while a worker referenced in this script is still active. Always wait for the named worker(s) to emit agent_stop first.
  
  Execute these steps in order (FOLLOW TO THE LETTER!):
  
  STEP 1 - DISPATCH:
  guidance
  
  Based on the above guidance and the work item details, select the best agent and thinking mode.
  
  PARALLELIZATION (pick the one matching your agent choice; append to --additional-context):
  - claude:
      "Independent sub-tasks MUST be parallelized via TeamCreate — one team, multiple workers in a single call. Sequential dispatch of independent work is a failure mode; default to TeamCreate whenever two or more sub-tasks have no data dependency."
  - codex:
      "When work decomposes into independent subtasks, immediately spawn bounded explorer/worker sub-agents for them and keep the critical path moving locally. Do not serialize non-blocking discovery, implementation, or verification; wait only when a result blocks integration, then merge/close agents."
  - gemini:
      "Mandate: Identify independent sub-tasks and concurrently delegate them to sub-agents using `invoke_agent` in a single turn. Ensure parallel sub-agents do not mutate the same files; otherwise, execute them simultaneously without setting `wait_for_previous`."
  
  Dispatch metadata: command="/next-build" args="test-slug" project="/project" subfolder="trees/test-slug"
  
  telec sessions run --command "/next-build" --args "test-slug" --project "/project"   --agent "<your selection>" --mode "<your selection>" --subfolder "trees/test-slug"
  Save the returned session_id.
  
  STEP 2 - START NON-BLOCKING HEARTBEAT TIMER AND INITIALIZE MARKER:
  Bash(command="sleep 300", run_in_background=true)
  Save the returned task_id.
  Save the current time as <marker_timestamp> for the tailing discipline.
  The timer runs in the background; notifications and timer completion arrive in your conversation.
  
  STEP 3 - WAIT:
  Tell the user: "Dispatched session <session_id>. Waiting for completion."
  Act on the next event that fires in your conversation — notification or timer completion.
  
  TAILING DISCIPLINE:
  - First tail: full window (no --since). Save the latest message timestamp as <marker_timestamp>.
  - All subsequent tails: use --since <marker_timestamp>. Update marker after each tail.
  Each telec sessions tail response includes `last_input_at`, `last_activity`,
  `last_agent_stop_at`, and computed `agent_status`.
  
  Status semantics:
  - `active`: `last_activity` exists and the latest observed activity is not the agent stop event.
  - `idle`: `last_activity` exists and `last_agent_stop_at == last_activity`.
  - `unknown`: no `last_activity` has been recorded yet.
  
  HEARTBEAT RULE:
  - On notification arrival or timer completion: tail the session (first time: full window; subsequent: --since <marker_timestamp>).
  - Update <marker_timestamp> to the latest message timestamp when new messages appear.
  - If `agent_status` is `active`: reset the non-blocking heartbeat timer and wait for the next event.
  - If `agent_status` is `idle`: proceed to the WHEN WORKER COMPLETES section below.
  - If `agent_status` is `unknown`: wait for the next event.
  
  FEEDBACK MESSAGES:
  - When sending a message to the worker because it needs feedback: cancel the old timer via KillShell(shell_id=<task_id>), start a new heartbeat timer via Bash(command="sleep 300", run_in_background=true), and save the new task_id.
  - Only send telec sessions send when there is actionable content: concrete gate failure details, a direct answer to a worker question, or a user-directed plan change.
  
  WHEN WORKER IDLES:
  Call telec todo work test-slug. The state machine emits the next action after the worker has stamped `telec todo stamp test-slug --build-complete`.
  
  ORCHESTRATION PRINCIPLE:
  You are an orchestrator. Execute the state machine's output verbatim. The state machine owns session lifecycle and dispatch decisions; phase is derived each call from stamped primitives (verdicts, approvals, skip stamps, drift review). Trust the process gates (pre-commit hooks, stamp clerical checks).
  
  NOTE: Prepared artifact contract for test-slug: PRD is the canonical intent and requirements source; implementation-plan is the execution spine; architecture and test-specs are optional context when present. Legacy requirements is only a fallback when PRD is absent. Start implementation now. When the build is committed and ready for review, run `telec todo stamp test-slug --build-complete`.
  '''
# ---
