# name: test_review_changes_requested_relay_message_addresses_every_finding
  '''
  REVIEW CHANGES REQUESTED: test-slug
  
  Execute in order:
  
  Tell the reviewer to start a direct conversation with the fixer:
  telec sessions send builder-1 "A fixer is active at builder-1. Start a direct conversation: telec sessions send builder-1 '<your findings summary>' --direct. Review requested changes for test-slug. Findings artifact: `review-findings`. Target: source code in the worktree. Required read: software-development/procedure/lifecycle/fix-review-findings. Address every Requirement-Violation, Critical, and Important finding — anything less keeps the verdict at REQUEST CHANGES per the severity schema in lifecycle/work/review. Requirement-Violation findings in particular indicate a stated requirement's success criteria are not satisfied in the delivery; fix the narrowing or the weak verification, do not argue severity. When every finding is resolved, commit the fixes and run `telec todo stamp test-slug --build-complete`. Read findings via: telec todo artifacts read test-slug review-findings Collaborate until all findings are resolved, then persist the full review-findings artifact with telec todo artifacts write test-slug review-findings <content> and set the verdict by arithmetic: APPROVE only when unresolved Requirement-Violation, Critical, and Important counts are all zero. Report FIX COMPLETE." (you will use regular send, NOT --direct)
  
  Cancel the old heartbeat timer via KillShell(shell_id=<task_id>).
  Start a new non-blocking heartbeat timer via Bash(command="sleep 300", run_in_background=true) and save the new task_id.
  Wait for fixer to complete (monitor via heartbeat; do not poll continuously).
  Wait for reviewer session builder-1 to report idle.
  When the signal arrives, call telec todo work test-slug.
  '''
# ---
